  "body": "### Fresh-log diagnosis\n- Bot 3 / Galaxy S25 was **not** out of capacity: backend explicitly allowed 2 new negotiations and 79 candidates were eligible. The catalog run then spent ~3 minutes per candidate waiting on `HumanVerificationHandler` after the offer modal failed to open.\n- The verification detector treated matching CAPTCHA/reCAPTCHA iframes in the DOM too broadly; hidden/background challenge widgets could stall a normal offer attempt.\n- Bot 4 / Galaxy Tab S11 Ultra also had capacity (5) but repeatedly received 0 DISCOVERED listings from the backend after scanning 96 results.\n- Backend marketplace `listingId` was globally UNIQUE and discovery de-duplicated IDs across every bot. That meant an item already seen by one bot could never be evaluated independently by another bot/configuration.\n- Two legacy `/api/negotiations` endpoints also assumed marketplace listing IDs were globally unique and therefore had to become bot-scoped together with the data model.\n\n### Changes\n- require a challenge iframe to be visibly rendered at meaningful dimensions before pausing for human verification\n- keep generic `Just a moment` / `Security check` markers title-only; visible body matching uses stronger human-verification phrases\n- log the exact verification evidence when a real challenge is detected\n- keep DOM/navigation read failures as inconclusive rather than CAPTCHA evidence\n- scope marketplace listing identity to `(bot_id, listing_id)` in JPA and repository discovery\n- add Flyway V29 migration that removes legacy global `listing_id` uniqueness and creates `uk_listing_bot_marketplace`\n- make legacy negotiation result/offer-sent lookups explicitly require `botId + listingId`, preventing cross-bot ambiguity\n- add regression tests for verification text strictness\n\n### Expected behavior\n- S25 catalog scans no longer freeze for 180 seconds merely because of a hidden challenge widget; a genuinely visible challenge still pauses safely for manual completion.\n- Different bots may independently discover/evaluate the same marketplace item. A bot still processes its own marketplace listing ID only once, preserving its historical terminal state/backlog behavior.\n- SEARCH_QUERY semantic filtering remains unchanged: S11 Ultra still rejects S10 FE+/wrong models/accessories.\n\n### Safety\n- no CAPTCHA is bypassed or automated\n- no offer quota/action guard is weakened\n- offer submission remains behind existing preflight, quota reservation and persistent real-action guards\n- existing listing history is preserved; no rows are deleted by the migration\n\n### Verification\n- latest CI run #252: Frontend ✅, Playwright unit tests ✅, Backend ✅",
